   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We get warnings since we need to reproject this shapefile object to a CRS in meters. This CRS should be a plane area to the specific zone of the shapefile ([more info](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/63004400/getting-a-userwarning-when-calculating-centroid-of-a-geoseries)). In the case of Peru, we use 24891 ([more info](https://epsg.io/24891)).\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 61,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "projected_dist_shp = dist_shp.to_crs( epsg = 24891 )\n",
    "\n",
    "projected_dist_shp[ 'centroids'] = projected_dist_shp.centroid"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Then, we reproject again the centroids to the original CRS."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 62,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "dist_shp[ 'Centroid_Latitude' ] = projected_dist_shp[ 'centroids' ].to_crs( epsg = 4326 ).y\n",
    "dist_shp[ 'Centroid_Longitude' ] = projected_dist_shp[ 'centroids' ].to_crs( epsg = 4326 ).x"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Intersection"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 71,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "health_centers = pd.read_csv( r\"../_data\\salud_places_peru.csv\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 72,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ht1 = health_centers[ health_centers.latitud != 0 ]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 73,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Make ht1 a geopandas\n",
    "ht1_geo = gpd.GeoDataFrame( ht1 , \n",
    "                           geometry= gpd.points_from_xy( \n",
    "                                      ht1.longitud, \n",
    "                                      ht1.latitud))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Check CRS\n",
    "\n",
    "We found that geolocation is recognized by google maps. We set the CRS that correspond to google maps."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 74,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ht1_geo_crs = ht1_geo.set_crs( epsg = 4326 )"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Find Ubigeo for each point"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 75,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Just take 10% of observations\n",
    "ht2_geo = ht1_geo_crs.sample( frac = 0.10 )"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 76,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Intersect with maps\n",
    "intersected_ht = gpd.overlay( ht2_geo , maps , how = 'intersection' )"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 77,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "ename": "AttributeError",
     "evalue": "'GeoDataFrame' object has no attribute 'IDDIST'",
     "output_type": "error",
     "traceback": [
      "\u001b[1;31m---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m",
